    "memoText": " \n                          VETO MESSAGE - No. 37\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 9031-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the  public authorities law, in relation to the\n      appointment of members of the Battery Park city authority\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would change the composition of the board  of  directors  of\nthe  Battery  Park  City Authority (\"BPCA\") by adding two more directors\nand requiring that a majority of the directors be residents  of  Battery\nPark City.\n \n  My  administration  is committed to good government that is responsive\nto the needs of communities served by the State's agencies and  authori-\nties.   However, this legislation presents risks to the effective admin-\nistration of BPCA.\n\n  The Legislature and the prior administration recently amended  Battery\nPark City's enabling legislation to ensure that residents' interests are\nrepresented  on  the board. Under current law, pursuant to a 2017 amend-\nment, at least two of the seven directors of BPCA  are  required  to  be\nresidents.\n \n  This  bill  could  give rise to increased conflicts of interest, which\nwould impede the Board's ability to manage its business  affairs  in  an\norderly  manner.  The  bill  also  restricts  the  Governor's ability to\nappoint, upon advice and consent of the  Senate,  the  candidates  whose\nexperience  and  qualifications  make  them  best suited to serve on the\nboard in a manner beneficial to the Battery Park City community.\n \n  For these reasons, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
    "vetoNumber": 37,
